§ `Ages on the life events`

-- c025: Chloe turns 18 on 2021-03-14.
#ASSERT `How old am I` 2003 3 14 2021 3 14 EQUALS 18
#ASSERT `How old am I` 2003 3 14 2021 3 13 EQUALS 17
-- k092: Jake on 2063-05-15.
#ASSERT `How old am I` 2006 8 30 2063 5 15 EQUALS 56

§ `s 4(3) -- presumed capable`

#ASSERT `Am I presumed capable` FALSE

§ `s 43 -- a guardian appointed for me`

#ASSERT `Can a guardian be appointed for me` 18 FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the Tribunal may appoint a guardian for me now`
-- c025: at 17 the Tribunal may already appoint, the appointment operating from the 18th birthday (s 43(2a), (2c)).
#ASSERT `Can a guardian be appointed for me` 17 FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the Tribunal may appoint a guardian for me from my 18th birthday`
-- k092: Jake, if his enduring guardian meets his needs (s 4(4)), cannot be given a guardian.
#ASSERT `Can a guardian be appointed for me` 56 FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `the Tribunal may not appoint a guardian for me`

§ `s 64 -- an administrator for my estate`

#ASSERT `Can an administrator be appointed for me` TRUE TRUE FALSE
-- An enduring power of attorney meeting the need is a less restrictive means (s 4(4)).
#ASSERT NOT (`Can an administrator be appointed for me` TRUE TRUE TRUE)

§ `ss 104(1a), 110B, 110P -- may I make it`

-- c025: Chloe at 18 may make all three.
#ASSERT `May I make the instrument` `an enduring power of attorney` 18 TRUE
-- c025: the day before, none.
#ASSERT NOT (`May I make the instrument` `an enduring power of attorney` 17 TRUE)
-- c091: Chloe at 60.
#ASSERT `May I make the instrument` `an enduring power of guardianship` 60 TRUE
-- c095: Chloe at 70.
#ASSERT `May I make the instrument` `an advance health directive` 70 TRUE
-- k092: Jake, if the stroke left him without full legal capacity.
#ASSERT NOT (`May I make the instrument` `an enduring power of attorney` 56 FALSE)
-- d090: Daniel at 78.
#ASSERT `May I make the instrument` `an advance health directive` 78 TRUE

§ `ss 104C, 110D -- whom may I appoint`

-- c082: Liam, 41, may be Chloe's attorney.
#ASSERT `May I appoint this person` `an enduring power of attorney` 41 TRUE
-- c082: Oliver, 10, may not.
#ASSERT NOT (`May I appoint this person` `an enduring power of attorney` 10 TRUE)
-- k092: Ruby, 30, may be Jake's enduring guardian.
#ASSERT `May I appoint this person` `an enduring power of guardianship` 30 TRUE
-- d085: Priya, 67, may be Daniel's attorney.
#ASSERT `May I appoint this person` `an enduring power of attorney` 67 TRUE

§ `s 104 -- my enduring power of attorney`

-- c082: Chloe at 37, one authorised witness and one other adult.
#ASSERT `Is my enduring power of attorney validly created` `Chloe's power to Liam` 37 TRUE
-- The donee cannot be the second witness (s 104(3)(b)).
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my enduring power of attorney validly created` `a power witnessed by an authorised witness and the donee` 37 TRUE)
-- Form 1: one of the paragraph 4 declarations must be deleted.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my enduring power of attorney validly created` `a power with both paragraph 4 declarations left in` 37 TRUE)
-- d085: Daniel at 69.
#ASSERT `Is my enduring power of attorney validly created` `Daniel's power to Priya` 69 TRUE
-- k092: Jake, if he lacked full legal capacity.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my enduring power of attorney validly created` `Jake's power to Ruby` 56 FALSE)

-- A continuing power is in force from execution (an inference).
#ASSERT `Is my enduring power of attorney in force` `a continuing power` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my enduring power of attorney in force` `a power that springs on a section 106 declaration` FALSE)

-- s 106 is only for the springing kind.
#ASSERT NOT (`Can the Tribunal declare I lack legal capacity` `a continuing power` TRUE)

#ASSERT `What is the most my attorney can be fined for not keeping records`  EQUALS 2000

-- While I am legally incapable, only through the Tribunal (s 107(1)(c), s 109(2)).
#ASSERT NOT (`May my attorney renounce` TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `May my attorney renounce` FALSE FALSE FALSE

#ASSERT `What happens to my power if an administrator is appointed` TRUE EQUALS `the Tribunal must revoke or vary my power to remove the inconsistency`

§ `s 110E -- my enduring power of guardianship`

-- c091.
#ASSERT `Is my enduring power of guardianship valid` `Chloe's enduring power of guardianship to Liam` 60 TRUE
-- Each acceptance needs two witnesses (s 110E(1)(f)).
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my enduring power of guardianship valid` `a power whose acceptance has only one witness` 60 TRUE)
-- d085.
#ASSERT `Is my enduring power of guardianship valid` `Daniel's enduring power of guardianship to Priya` 69 TRUE

§ `ss 110F, 110G, 45 -- what my enduring guardian may decide`

-- Not while I can judge for myself (s 110F).
#ASSERT NOT (`May my enduring guardian act for me now` FALSE TRUE)

-- c091: where Chloe lives, once she cannot judge.
#ASSERT `May my enduring guardian make this decision` `where I live` TRUE FALSE
-- c091: an estate matter, not the person (an inference).
#ASSERT NOT (`May my enduring guardian make this decision` `selling my house` TRUE FALSE)
-- Not while she can judge.
#ASSERT NOT (`May my enduring guardian make this decision` `a treatment decision other than about an abortion` FALSE FALSE)
-- s 45(4).
#ASSERT NOT (`May my enduring guardian make this decision` `making a will for me` TRUE FALSE)
-- Schedule 1, section 4B(h).
#ASSERT `May my enduring guardian make this decision` `which support services I have access to` TRUE FALSE

-- Schedule 1, section 3B kept.
#ASSERT NOT (`May my surviving joint enduring guardians act` TRUE)

§ `regs 7, 9 -- the prescribed directive form`

-- c095.
#ASSERT `Was my directive form prescribed` `the current Schedule 2 form` 2073 3 14
-- c095: the old form is long out of date.
#ASSERT NOT (`Was my directive form prescribed` `the Schedule 2 form of the former regulations` 2073 3 14)
-- Last day of the transitional period.
#ASSERT `Was my directive form prescribed` `the Schedule 2 form of the former regulations` 2023 2 3
#ASSERT NOT (`Was my directive form prescribed` `the Schedule 2 form of the former regulations` 2023 2 4)

§ `ss 110P, 110Q, 110R -- my directive`

-- c095.
#ASSERT `Is my advance health directive valid` `Chloe's directive at 70` 70 TRUE
-- s 110Q(2).
#ASSERT `Is my advance health directive valid` `a directive made without the maker being encouraged to seek advice` 70 TRUE
-- s 110P; Schedule 2.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my advance health directive valid` `a directive with no treatment decisions in Part 4` 70 TRUE)
-- k096.
#ASSERT `Is my advance health directive valid` `Jake's directive at 68` 68 TRUE

-- Made under coercion (s 110R(1)(b)).
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my treatment decision valid` TRUE TRUE TRUE)

§ `ss 110S, 110T -- operation and revocation`

-- A later enduring power of guardianship is not by itself a change of mind (s 110T).
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my treatment decision revoked` TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- Schedule 2's statement revoking prior directives.
#ASSERT `Is my treatment decision revoked` FALSE FALSE TRUE

#ASSERT `Does my treatment decision operate` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- Unanticipated circumstances that would change a reasonable person's mind (s 110S(3)).
#ASSERT NOT (`Does my treatment decision operate` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE)

-- Assumed by s 108(2)(b) (an inference).
#ASSERT `How can my instrument be revoked` `an enduring power of attorney` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `I may revoke it myself`
-- s 110N.
#ASSERT `How can my instrument be revoked` `an enduring power of guardianship` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the Act gives the Tribunal power to revoke it and is silent on revocation by me`

§ `s 110ZD -- my person responsible`

-- k092, on the supposition that Jake has no spouse or partner: Ruby, his adult child.
#ASSERT `Who is my nearest relative` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `my child`

-- k092: Ruby on Carer Allowance is still unpaid (s 110ZD(6)).
#ASSERT `Is my carer my unpaid primary carer` 30 TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my carer my unpaid primary carer` 30 TRUE TRUE)

#ASSERT `Who is my person responsible` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `my nearest relative who is close to me`
#ASSERT `Who is my person responsible` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no person responsible`

§ `ss 110ZJ, 119 -- who decides`

-- k096: Jake's directive outranks Ruby as enduring guardian.
#ASSERT `Who decides my treatment` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `the treatment decision in my directive`
-- k092: no directive covering the treatment; Ruby decides.
#ASSERT `Who decides my treatment` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `my enduring guardian`
-- c095: Chloe's directive outranks Liam.
#ASSERT `Who decides my treatment` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `the treatment decision in my directive`
#ASSERT `Who decides my treatment` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `my guardian`
#ASSERT `Who decides my treatment` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `my person responsible`

#ASSERT `Who decides my other personal matters` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `my enduring guardian`
-- s 119 names no person responsible.
#ASSERT `Who decides my other personal matters` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no-one under the section`

